  <div id="tab-units" class="tab-panel">

    <div class="unit-type-grid">

      <div class="unit-type-card">
        <div class="unit-type-header">
          <span class="unit-type-name">Infantry</span>
          <span class="unit-type-sub">Creature</span>
        </div>
        <p>Follows all standard rules without exceptions. The baseline unit type.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="unit-type-card">
        <div class="unit-type-header">
          <span class="unit-type-name">Bike</span>
          <span class="unit-type-sub">Creature</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Cannot move vertically on terrain.</li>
          <li>Auto-advances 6″ on Advance order.</li>
          <li>May fire Heavy weapons with Move &amp; Shoot.</li>
          <li>Always fires Rapid Fire up to full range.</li>
          <li>Fires all weapon types on Charge at −1.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="unit-type-card">
        <div class="unit-type-header">
          <span class="unit-type-name">Character Model</span>
          <span class="unit-type-sub">Creature</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Can join a creature unit (start Command Phase within 2″). One order is issued for both.</li>
          <li>One character per unit. Cannot join Monstrous Creatures or Vehicles.</li>
          <li>Auto-rallies during Rally Phase if not attached. Always uses its own armour/ward save, even when attached.</li>
          <li>Fires one weapon, or two pistols, per activation (unless equipment grants another).</li>
          <li><strong>Attached:</strong> character and unit count as a single unit, but the character does not count towards the unit's starting strength.</li>
          <li><strong>Attached:</strong> cannot be assigned ranged wounds unless the unit is completely destroyed.</li>
          <li><strong>Attached:</strong> character and unit determine Engagement Range separately and are targeted separately in melee — attacks on one cannot affect the other.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="unit-type-card">
        <div class="unit-type-header">
          <span class="unit-type-name">Jet Bike</span>
          <span class="unit-type-sub">Creature</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Can move over (enemy) units and terrain.</li>
          <li>Ignores terrain movement and vertical movement costs.</li>
          <li>Auto-advances 6″ on Advance order.</li>
          <li>May fire Heavy weapons with Move &amp; Shoot.</li>
          <li>Always fires Rapid Fire up to full range.</li>
          <li>Fires all weapon types on Charge at −1.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="unit-type-card">
        <div class="unit-type-header">
          <span class="unit-type-name">Jump Pack Infantry</span>
          <span class="unit-type-sub">Creature</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Can move over (enemy) units and terrain.</li>
          <li>Ignores terrain movement and vertical movement costs.</li>
          <li>Gains the Deep Strike special rule.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="unit-type-card">
        <div class="unit-type-header">
          <span class="unit-type-name">Monstrous Creature</span>
          <span class="unit-type-sub">Creature</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Cannot be joined by a Character Model.</li>
          <li>Cannot enter transport vehicles.</li>
          <li>Gains a +3 bonus on Armor penetration rolls.</li>
          <li>May fire Heavy with Move &amp; Shoot. Always Rapid Fire up to full range. All types on Charge at −1.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="unit-type-card">
        <div class="unit-type-header">
          <span class="unit-type-name">Monstrous Infantry</span>
          <span class="unit-type-sub">Creature</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Cannot be joined by a Character Model.</li>
          <li>Cannot enter transport vehicles.</li>
          <li>Gains a +2 bonus on Armor penetration rolls.</li>
          <li>May fire Heavy with Move &amp; Shoot. Always Rapid Fire up to full range. All types on Charge at −1.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="unit-type-card">
        <div class="unit-type-header">
          <span class="unit-type-name">Walker</span>
          <span class="unit-type-sub">Vehicle</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Treated like vehicles but locked in melee like infantry.</li>
          <li>May change facing during its own initiative step in melee.</li>
          <li>No Defensive Fire against enemies charging from behind the torso's facing.</li>
          <li>May fire Heavy with Move &amp; Shoot. Always Rapid Fire up to full range. All types on Charge at −1.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="unit-type-card">
        <div class="unit-type-header">
          <span class="unit-type-name">Vehicle</span>
          <span class="unit-type-sub">Vehicle</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Has Front/Side/Rear armour values and Hull Points.</li>
          <li>Auto-passes Leadership tests.</li>
          <li>Tank Shock on Charge: 1 auto hit per inch travelled at Initiative 10.</li>
          <li>Not locked in melee — may leave freely, but while in melee may only be given Advance, Fight or Move &amp; Shoot.</li>
          <li>Cannot shoot if enemy is in base contact.</li>
          <li>Turret weapons: 360°. Chassis weapons: 180°. A weapon is only 360° if firing all the way round would never force the model itself to turn (and so change its armour facings).</li>
          <li>Move &gt;12″: cannot fire any weapons. Move 6–12″: fire 1 weapon.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="unit-type-card unit-type-card--wide">
        <div class="unit-type-header">
          <span class="unit-type-name">Flyer</span>
          <span class="unit-type-sub">Vehicle</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Deployed during Reinforcement phase, anywhere on the battlefield.</li>
          <li>Can only receive Advance (fire 1 weapon) or Move &amp; Shoot (fire all weapons) orders. Cannot activate first in a turn.</li>
          <li>Always counts as having moved 24″ when not in Hover Mode.</li>
          <li>Subtract 12″ from weapon range when shooting at or from flyers. −1 hit penalty when targeting flyers.</li>
          <li>On Advance order: 4+ ward save. Cannot engage or be engaged in melee.</li>
          <li>3 permanent Engine Damage = disabled for one full round, then all Engine Damage removed and redeployed.</li>
          <li><strong>Hover Mode:</strong> Can capture/hold/contest objectives. Must start in hover mode during deployment or enter by not repositioning in reserve phase.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Vehicle Facing &amp; Firing Arcs</span></div>
      <div class="diagram-box">
        <img class="diagram-svg" src="/diagrams/armour-facing.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             alt="Vehicle armour facings seen from above: front, two sides and rear, divided by 45 degree lines from the hull corners." />
        <div class="diagram-legend"><span>Hits resolve against the facing the attacker touches</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-box">
        <img class="diagram-svg" src="/diagrams/weapon-arc-turret.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             alt="A turret-mounted weapon fires through a full 360 degree arc." />
        <div class="diagram-legend"><span><strong>Turret-mounted</strong> — 360&deg;</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-box">
        <img class="diagram-svg" src="/diagrams/weapon-arc-chassis.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             alt="A chassis-mounted weapon fires only through a 180 degree forward arc." />
        <div class="diagram-legend"><span><strong>Chassis-mounted</strong> — 180&deg; forward</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Transports</span></div>
      <p><strong>Embarking:</strong> a unit within 3&Prime; at the end of its movement can board a transport. Passengers cannot be given a <strong>Stand &amp; Shoot</strong> order. Any number of units may ride, up to the vehicle&rsquo;s transport capacity.</p>
      <p>What the passengers may do depends on how far the transport moved this activation:</p>
      <table class="ref-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Vehicle moved</th><th>Passenger actions</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>0&Prime;</td><td>Use fire hatches <em>or</em> disembark within 3&Prime;. Execute their command normally.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>&gt;0&Prime;–6&Prime;</td><td>Use fire hatches <em>or</em> disembark within 3&Prime;. Execute their command. <strong>Cannot move or Charge.</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>&gt;6&Prime;–12&Prime;</td><td>Use fire hatches <em>or</em> disembark within 3&Prime;. Execute their command at <strong>&minus;1 to hit</strong> until the end of the battle round. <strong>Cannot move or Charge.</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>&gt;12&Prime;</td><td><strong>No actions at all.</strong></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="note"><strong>Fire Hatches:</strong> each one lets a single passenger fire their weapon when the unit activates. A vehicle with the <strong>Open</strong> rule has fire hatches equal to its passenger capacity — and its passengers can be shot at, count as physically on the battlefield for ranges and psychic powers (measured from the hull), share the transport&rsquo;s cover, cannot fight in melee from inside, and can always make a 6&Prime; Charge move after disembarking if the vehicle moved up to 12&Prime;.</p>
      <p class="note">A transport and the units inside it count as <strong>one reserve</strong>: a single 4+ brings them on together. For what happens when the transport is destroyed, see <strong>Vehicle Destruction</strong> under Combat.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Profile Values Reference</span></div>
      <div class="stat-ref-grid">
        <div class="stat-ref"><img src="/stat-icons/move.svg" class="stat-icon" alt="M"><div><strong>Movement</strong> — Speed in inches. "−" = cannot move.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><img src="/stat-icons/weapon-skill.svg" class="stat-icon" alt="WS"><div><strong>Weapon Skill</strong> — Melee hit roll target. "−" = cannot fight in melee. Max 1+.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><img src="/stat-icons/ballistic-skill.svg" class="stat-icon" alt="BS"><div><strong>Ballistic Skill</strong> — Ranged hit roll target. "−" = cannot shoot. Max 1+.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><img src="/stat-icons/strength.svg" class="stat-icon" alt="S"><div><strong>Strength</strong> — Melee wounding power. Max 10 or D.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><img src="/stat-icons/toughness.svg" class="stat-icon" alt="T"><div><strong>Toughness</strong> — Damage resistance. Max 10.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><img src="/stat-icons/wounds.svg" class="stat-icon" alt="W"><div><strong>Wounds</strong> — Damage capacity. Excess damage doesn't carry over between models.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><img src="/stat-icons/initiative.svg" class="stat-icon" alt="I"><div><strong>Initiative</strong> — Melee activation order, highest first. Max 10.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><img src="/stat-icons/attacks.svg" class="stat-icon" alt="A"><div><strong>Attacks</strong> — Melee attacks per activation. "−" = cannot fight in melee. Max 10.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><img src="/stat-icons/leadership.svg" class="stat-icon" alt="Ld"><div><strong>Leadership</strong> — Bravery. Uses highest in squad including attached characters. Max 10.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><img src="/stat-icons/save.svg" class="stat-icon" alt="Sv"><div><strong>Save</strong> — Armour protection, modified by weapon AP. Roll of 1 always fails. Max 1+.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><span class="stat-letter">Inv</span><div><strong>Ward Save</strong> — Not affected by AP. Max 4+ (unless stated otherwise).</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Modifying Profile Values</span></div>
      <p><strong>Order of modifications</strong> — additive first (<strong>+1</strong>), then multiplicative (<strong>×2</strong>), then subtractive (<strong>&minus;1</strong>). The order matters: the same three modifiers applied in another order give a different number.</p>
      <table class="ref-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Example</th><th>Applies as</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Several instances of the <em>same rule</em></td><td>A model with a Storm shield targeted by Shrouded</td><td>Only the highest modifier</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Several instances of the <em>same equipment</em></td><td>A unit with two models carrying a Trophy</td><td>Only the highest modifier</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Several instances that <em>say</em> they are cumulative</td><td>An Eldar Fire blade</td><td>Combined</td></tr>
          <tr><td><em>Different</em> rules and equipment</td><td>The Terrifying rule plus a Trophy</td><td>Combined</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="note"><strong>Modifying Strength:</strong> if a model&rsquo;s Strength changes, it gains a temporary minimum AT value in melee unless it is already as good or better. At <strong>Strength 7 or higher</strong> all its melee attacks have <strong>AT(1)</strong>, again unless already better.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Profile Value Tests</span></div>
      <p>Some rules call for a test against a profile value — a &ldquo;Toughness test&rdquo;, a &ldquo;Leadership value test&rdquo;. Roll <strong>1D6</strong>. The roll must be <strong>equal to or below</strong> the value to pass, and a roll of <strong>6 always fails</strong>. Use the <em>current</em> value, after any equipment, psychic power or other modifier.</p>
      <p class="note">Not the same thing as the Leadership test for Battleshock, which is <strong>2D6</strong> against Leadership. The opposite convention applies to attacks: on a hit or wound roll a <strong>6 always succeeds</strong> whatever the target number, while an armour save of <strong>1 always fails</strong>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Weapon Profile Reference</span></div>
      <div class="stat-ref-grid">
        <div class="stat-ref"><span class="stat-letter">Rng</span><div><strong>Range</strong> — Maximum distance in inches, measured from the model's base (or, lacking one, any part of the hull). A “−” means melee only.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><span class="stat-letter">Typ</span><div><strong>Type</strong> — Assault, Grenade, Heavy, Melee, Pistol or Rapid Fire. Ranged weapons only shoot and Melee weapons only fight, unless stated otherwise.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><span class="stat-letter">S</span><div><strong>Strength</strong> — 1–10, or <strong>D</strong> for a Destroyer weapon. <strong>U</strong> means the wielder's own Strength; a modifier (“+1”, “x2”) applies to it.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><span class="stat-letter">AP</span><div><strong>Armor Piercing</strong> — How far it reduces the target's armour save. AP −3 is better than AP −1; AP 0 applies no modifier.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><span class="stat-letter">D</span><div><strong>Damage</strong> — Damage inflicted by a successful attack, after failed saves.</div></div>
        <div class="stat-ref"><span class="stat-letter">Abl</span><div><strong>Abilities</strong> — Special rules for the weapon; see the Weapon Abilities section below, the Codex, or the army list entry.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Base Sizes</span></div>
      <ul class="notes-list">
        <li>Creatures <strong>must</strong> use the base size supplied with the official model.</li>
        <li>Vehicles <strong>may</strong> use the base size supplied with the official model.</li>
        <li>Conversions, kitbashes and original creations must use the same base size as the official model.</li>
        <li>If a resculpt ships with a bigger base than the old version, you may use either size for your old model.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-section reveal">
      <div class="section-divider"><span>Weapon Types</span></div>
      <table class="weapon-types-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Stand &amp; Shoot</th>
            <th>Move &amp; Shoot</th>
            <th>Advance</th>
            <th>Charge</th>
            <th>Fight</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><img src="/weapon-type-icons/assault.svg" class="wtype-icon" alt=""> Assault</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/weapon-type-icons/grenade.svg" class="wtype-icon" alt=""> Grenade¹</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓*</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/weapon-type-icons/heavy.svg" class="wtype-icon" alt=""> Heavy</td><td>✓</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/weapon-type-icons/melee.svg" class="wtype-icon" alt=""> Melee²</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/weapon-type-icons/pistol.svg" class="wtype-icon" alt=""> Pistol³</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>—</td></tr>
          <tr><td><img src="/weapon-type-icons/rapid-fire.svg" class="wtype-icon" alt=""> Rapid Fire⁴</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <ul class="notes-list">
        <li>¹ One model per unit may use a grenade. In melee, grenades can only target Vehicles or Monstrous Creatures.</li>
        <li>² If a model has at least one melee weapon AND one pistol, gains +1 Attack in melee.</li>
        <li>³ A model can fire up to two pistols, OR other eligible weapons (not both).</li>
        <li>⁴ Doubles its attacks against a target within half range. Without a Stand &amp; Shoot order it can only fire at targets within half range.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div><!-- /tab-units -->


