          <ul>
            <li>Allied units are treated as friendly in all respects.</li>
            <li>Auras and psychic powers can be cast on allied units.</li>
            <li>Transport vehicles can carry units from both factions freely.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="alliance-card alliance-card--y">
          <div class="alliance-badge"><span class="dot dot-y"></span> Allies of Convenience</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Allied units are treated as separate armies.</li>
            <li>Auras and psychic powers only affect the primary faction's units.</li>
            <li>Transports can only carry units of the primary faction.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="alliance-card alliance-card--r">
          <div class="alliance-badge"><span class="dot dot-r"></span> Desperate Allies</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Same restrictions as Allies of Convenience, plus:</li>
            <li>Units within 12″ of the ally must pass a Ld test (−1) or lose their order for that turn.</li>
            <li>Uses own mini-AOP: 0–1 HQ · 1–2 Troops · 0–1 Elite/FA/HS per Troop · 0–ᵀ Transports.</li>
            <li>Cannot select a second AOP after filling all slots.</li>
            <li>May select own Army Customisation options.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">A faction may always ally with itself. Two Inquisition forces or two Dark Eldar Kabals allied together count as Allies of Convenience (Y), not Battle Brothers.</p>
